{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776387062,"nonce":"kQFGc/TGf+78ZXEmETMxmih6WRA=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM7_EoUr","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/58","origin":"github"},"title":"Add BT/Nav2 action-status topics to rosbag logger for post-deployment debrief","message":"## Summary\n\nAdd BT / Nav2 action-status and planning topics to the BizzyBoat\nrosbag logger config so that autonomy decisions can be reconstructed\nfrom bag files during post-deployment debrief.\n\n## Motivation\n\nDuring the 2026-04-16 field test, `/rosout` showed 20× planner aborts,\n9× BT task aborts, and multiple hover engage/disengage cycles — but the\nbags couldn't answer what goal was commanded, what the BT decided, what\npath was planned, or why the planner aborted. Diagnosis required live\nobservation and the deployment log.\n\nFor unattended autonomous runs (the end goal — autonomous round-trip\nsurveys), this won't be available. The action-status topics are tiny\nmessages that would make post-mortems self-contained.\n\n## Proposed topics\n\n| Topic | Type | Why | Bandwidth |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `/bizzy/run_tasks/_action/goal` | action goal | **Primary** — what task/mission was commanded | tiny |\n| `/bizzy/run_tasks/_action/status` | GoalStatusArray | Task lifecycle: accepted → executing → aborted/succeeded | tiny |\n| `/bizzy/run_tasks/_action/feedback` | action feedback | Progress during execution | tiny |\n| `/bizzy/compute_path_through_poses/_action/status` | GoalStatusArray | Planner success/abort timing | tiny |\n| `/bizzy/follow_path/_action/status` | GoalStatusArray | Controller success/abort timing | tiny |\n| `/bizzy/hover/_action/status` | GoalStatusArray | Hover engage/disengage timing | tiny |\n| `/bizzy/plan` | nav_msgs/Path | Planned path output | small |\n| `/bizzy/behavior_tree_log` | nav2_msgs/BehaviorTreeLog | BT node state transitions (decision chain) | small |\n| `/bizzy/goal_pose` | PoseStamped | External goal input | tiny |\n\nAll action-status topics are a few bytes per state transition —\nnegligible bandwidth and storage impact compared to the existing\n10 Hz sensor streams.\n\n## What this enables\n\nWith these topics in the bag, a post-deployment debrief can reconstruct:\n\n- \"Task X was commanded at time T, accepted, executing for N seconds,\n  then aborted\" (run_tasks action)\n- \"Planner attempted path, failed due to TF extrapolation, BT fell\n  back to hover, hover engaged for M seconds, then new goal arrived\"\n  (BT log + action statuses)\n- \"Controller was following this path (plan topic) when it aborted\n  after the PID diverged\" (follow_path status + plan)\n\nvs today's \"something failed 20 times\" from rosout alone.\n\n## Implementation\n\nAdd the topic list to the logger section of `bizzyboat.yaml`\n(currently at line 246+). The topics need to be verified against\nthe actual running system first — action names and namespacing may\ndiffer from the stock Nav2 defaults.\n\nNote: `/bizzy/behavior_tree_log` may require enabling in the\nBT navigator node config (e.g., `enable_groot_monitoring: true`\nor similar) — check if this is already active.\n\n## Related\n\n- Deployment debrief skill: [ros2_agent_workspace#435](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_agent_workspace/issues/435) — these topics would go into the \"should be logged\" reference list\n- 2026-04-16 deployment log session (hover v1–v4 debugging, planner TF extrapolation bug)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `claude-opus-4-6[1m]`","files":null}]}